{"timestamp":"2026-01-15T21:52:56.107Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Planning fallback auth path for codex sync**\n\nI'm deciding to adjust the codex auth target path fallback to a host-writable directory under `.docker-git/secrets/codex-host/<projectId>` when `.orch` isn't writable, aligning UID 1000 permissions and updating config to mount and create that path. This should fix the sync skipping and authorization error."}}
{"timestamp":"2026-01-15T21:52:56.107Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Designing multi-level fallback for codex auth path**\n\nI'm finalizing a three-tier fallback in `resolveProjectCodexTarget`—original path, project fallback, then shared global path—checking writability sequentially and updating config if fallback chosen, else failing with clear error; this ensures codex auth syncing won’t silently skip due to permission issues."}}
