{"timestamp":"2026-01-16T09:43:03.104Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Explaining config.toml trust update**\n\nThe config was updated to include a config.toml specifying trusted projects and approval policy, fixing the missing trust setup since config.yml doesn't set trust. The prompt appeared because Codex run from an untrusted directory (/home/dev/.codex) before the fix; now the config.toml includes trust entries for relevant paths and approval_policy=never. The container was restarted to apply changes. If prompts persist when running in other directories, add those paths to the trusted list in config.toml."}}
{"timestamp":"2026-01-16T09:43:03.104Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Clarifying prompts and config changes**\n\nThe \"need network access to fetch curated skills list\" prompt is a per-command Codex permission suppressed by approval_policy=never in config.toml. If prompts persist, Codex might be running outside trusted paths or reading defaults. We updated `src/server/codex.ts`, `templates.ts`, and `http.ts` to always write config.toml with trust entries for relevant directories and approval_policy=never. After rebuilding and recreating the container, config.toml exists inside both host and container paths, suppressing prompts. The Codex server was started in the background and can be stopped with kill if needed. Next steps: run Codex from `/home/dev/app` to verify no prompts, and if prompts appear in other directories, add those to the trusted paths in config.toml."}}
{"timestamp":"2026-01-16T09:43:03.104Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"reasoning","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Explaining config.toml trust update**\n\nThe config was updated to include a config.toml specifying trusted projects and approval policy, fixing the missing trust setup since config.yml doesn't set trust. The prompt appeared because Codex run from an untrusted directory (/home/dev/.codex) before the fix; now the config.toml includes trust entries for relevant paths and approval_policy=never. The container was restarted to apply changes. If prompts persist when running in other directories, add those paths to the trusted list in config.toml."},{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Clarifying prompts and config changes**\n\nThe \"need network access to fetch curated skills list\" prompt is a per-command Codex permission suppressed by approval_policy=never in config.toml. If prompts persist, Codex might be running outside trusted paths or reading defaults. We updated `src/server/codex.ts`, `templates.ts`, and `http.ts` to always write config.toml with trust entries for relevant directories and approval_policy=never. After rebuilding and recreating the container, config.toml exists inside both host and container paths, suppressing prompts. The Codex server was started in the background and can be stopped with kill if needed. Next steps: run Codex from `/home/dev/app` to verify no prompts, and if prompts appear in other directories, add those to the trusted paths in config.toml."}],"content":null,"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABpaggctttrUA932jWCT6osU_8pO0sJPxVA6PPsD8qX0_twdzqmi2O92sp4RMjtI5lempgexmOOgtfn9kthPMFbOIhydEEIUKAaDINQs9pGy5FnDaw7bcr5qPyAeefcVpYiE3bITcGMysAcS8pDdMz6psr3P712QVA2yoB3fY7Np4Nvir672mkfzW0bAN5Fm1Gt07G9dcR2wE2sbNciPIRS9qkr-51XfV3KFK1upO6RV2ciAN48LI_9fbXMXUNWoK_Vnc4Qu4y6z-k0myiX0ek5gp2J2OCnQc4aDy3ti5wEuF5OQiR0avXte1tU9T2oIX5JIn8y_lVpWJaqp3-Vj6a3IW5nHSuVab3dXbZO8o3CeZZrc8ojity6PXz1u2CjlM8WIZbZpceumdirNYYL8xjOGhb_xGzxS_edyhw-8H9e