{"timestamp":"2026-01-16T10:44:08.377Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Clarifying sudo vs approval prompts**\n\nSudo prompts are disabled globally via NOPASSWD in the Dockerfile, while Codex approval prompts come from its own trust and approval policy settings. Adding trust entries and setting approval_policy to \"never\" in config.toml prevents Codex from asking for command approvals in the project directory."}}
{"timestamp":"2026-01-16T10:44:08.377Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Explaining Codex prompts and sudo setup**\n\nThe Codex prompt for command approval is separate from sudo password requests; it arises from Codex’s trust and approval policies. We added a config.toml (not just config.yml) to mark `/home/dev`, `/home/dev/app`, and `/home/dev/.codex` as trusted, and set approval_policy to \"never\" to disable approvals. Passwordless sudo was enabled globally via Dockerfile and verified with `sudo -n true` for the dev user. To apply changes fully, the user needs to recreate the container so the updated config and Dockerfile take effect. If prompts persist, ensure Codex runs from a trusted directory or add the path to the trust list in config.toml."}}
{"timestamp":"2026-01-16T10:44:08.377Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"reasoning","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Clarifying sudo vs approval prompts**\n\nSudo prompts are disabled globally via NOPASSWD in the Dockerfile, while Codex approval prompts come from its own trust and approval policy settings. Adding trust entries and setting approval_policy to \"never\" in config.toml prevents Codex from asking for command approvals in the project directory."},{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Explaining Codex prompts and sudo setup**\n\nThe Codex prompt for command approval is separate from sudo password requests; it arises from Codex’s trust and approval policies. We added a config.toml (not just config.yml) to mark `/home/dev`, `/home/dev/app`, and `/home/dev/.codex` as trusted, and set approval_policy to \"never\" to disable approvals. Passwordless sudo was enabled globally via Dockerfile and verified with `sudo -n true` for the dev user. To apply changes fully, the user needs to recreate the container so the updated config and Dockerfile take effect. If prompts persist, ensure Codex runs from a trusted directory or add the path to the trust list in config.toml."}],"content":null,"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABpahZthmOcwC2KXWH21UrG2Be3VFzO4Gen0jRzq63oh3A7ydiGtU4dYMFVop2CJyOgaH2IHqUnVkxifKbyVUjIPuxN03QAGXkS0sDc-EBF5EeRiLHIjd0goB3y9_aEy-hH8qec1mLoM-D8UolB4JXd3ZAuHOYO2PdBPLQTrqvNGICuY9JrSUdy4tsogHIUXYTGPtHagjQwCBBkT4da5AwtlgFaV9eMirDPh-tXflDWM4uRmjfzi-ayugSrj0GNdveKS3tVshmAu3LgirH6jIpdZriBJ1yaKWPL3WY7EZs2x6Q2v1QCL9PoZ_O1duRkCxW0w3mCh4t4PHtNkfGBPeQKT_d680Qpl4iNaE5ZjttZG4gUEACFgSnkoNlth2_hHRUpQZHefwBL_4H8bpN_mKBXnlet7hxf9iYMa7OfT9yojNNC87RyDwZWkPZbWsXAX6QUKJOgt1o0tWycVJDhKAdWhP1izblVN-OcyS_TF6jeLGBte76OAjhMCE1eyI_XIQAITWViCNMuJEzVPRdeZSfpJKDXulkpn6xOMxWAHP30k0Bmnr4gEEw3FyJOG_ELZqMZrsEtpzLPthZ_cPPwUYWdJmZZh-quctN_s1DeQOALZJ4046r8JM1NWj2S-yc4c8nMpJNjWj1uhRD9pjqKXAM3YPkYfasjmxTwdZhlHhYC3qcBUm_5HVqCX_rVuNRGMLS_mWH56FVX-YbXdTHkgI499HRKv_Tp5axh-soE_Ol47F1XR8HR